-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Split Iff
-- statement:
--   **The full half-sandwich relation is equivalent to its head-tail form.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, let $k\in\mathbb N$, and let $\delta$ be an error threshold. Let $L_{k+1}$ and $R_{k+1}$ denote the full left and right half-sandwich families on $(k+1)$-tuples of slice points. Let $O_k$ and $R_k$ denote the corresponding head-tail families on one slice question together with a $k$-tuple of tail points, with the completed head effect placed before or after the tail half-product on the left register.
--
--   Write $\mathcal Q$ for the finite set of slice questions. Then the two state-dependent operator-distance assertions are equivalent:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^{k+1})}
--   \!\left(L_{k+1},R_{k+1};\delta\right)
--   \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q\times\mathbb{F}_q^k)}
--   \!\left(O_k,R_k;\delta\right).
--   $$
--
--   The equivalence follows from the uniform point-tuple decomposition and the corresponding outcome reindexing. It is the bridge between the global half-sandwich statement and the head-tail estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_split_iff`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
